digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56657-5
  rankdir="TB";
  "N16" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Reasoning: Given cFLIP/vFLIP inhibit apoptosis and vFLIPs use DEDs, therefore DED mimicry inhibits death."];
  "N18" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-Reasoning: Given DNA triggers signaling and proteins not reported, therefore protein-mediated interaction is a gap."];
  "N2" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Reasoning: Given transition causes candidiasis and candidiasis has high mortality, therefore transition is severe."];
  "N9" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Reasoning: Given Als3 is abundant and Als3 induces immune response, therefore Als3 is a key immune modulator."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate whether the hypha-specific Candida albicans protein Als3 engages host death-effector-domain DEDs in FADD and caspase-8, in a viral FLIP-like manner, to modulate immune signaling and cell-death pathways that contribute to intestinal inflammation.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) The retained and repaired terminal conclusions jointly motivate the paper-level research proposal."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Death-effector-domain-related signaling, including FADD/caspase-8 complexes, is relevant to inflammation and cell-death pathways."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) Caspase-8/FADD loss is associated with colitis, and caspase-8 activation can trigger IL-1β secretion, placing these proteins in contexts relevant to intestinal inflammation and immune signaling."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) FADD/caspase-8 DED-related signaling provides a plausible host pathway context for studying gut inflammation, immune signaling, and cell-death pathways."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) Because FADD/caspase-8 DED-related signaling is relevant to gut inflammation and cell-death pathways, and viral FLIP-like proteins can use DED-DED interactions to inhibit apoptosis, DED interactions are a plausible mechanistic target for investigation."];
  "R20" [label="(0,0,0) Given the gap in reported Candida albicans protein interactions with intracellular host components and the plausibility of DED interactions as a mechanistic target, a novel C. albicans protein-DED interaction is a reasonable hypothesis to investigate."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) Because Als3 is an abundant hypha-specific immune-modulating protein and Candida albicans protein-DED interactions are a plausible hypothesis, Als3 is a reasonable candidate to test for interaction with host DED-containing proteins."];
  "R22" [label="(0,0,0) Hyphal Als3 interacts with the DEDs of FADD and caspase-8 and resembles DED-containing viral FLIP-like proteins, supporting a mimicry-like hypothesis rather than conclusively proving mimicry."];
  "R23" [label="(0,0,0) The observation that Als3 engages FADD/caspase-8 DEDs supports extending Candida albicans immune-recognition studies from extracellular factors toward intracellular host signaling interfaces."];
  "R24" [label="(0,0,0) A supported paper-level proposal is that hyphal Candida albicans Als3 should be investigated as a host-interacting fungal protein that engages the DEDs of FADD and caspase-8 and may modulate viral-FLIP-like immune signaling and cell-death pathways relevant to intestinal inflammation."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) High-damaging Candida albicans strains that form hyphae are associated with exacerbated intestinal inflammation, and this association can be considered within the broader context that C. albicans can become an opportunistic pathogen linked to serious candidiasis."];
  "S11" [label="(11,0,0) Observation: Als3 is the most abundant hypha-specific protein."];
  "S12" [label="(12,0,0) General Rule: Als3 induces immune responses promoting clearance."];
  "S13" [label="(13,0,0) Observation: DEDs regulate inflammation and cell death."];
  "S14" [label="(14,0,0) General Rule: FADD/Caspase-8 complex regulates cell death pathways."];
  "S15" [label="(15,0,0) Observation: Caspase-8/Fadd ablation leads to colitis."];
  "S16" [label="(16,0,0) General Rule: Caspase-8 activation triggers IL-1β secretion."];
  "S19" [label="(19,0,0) Observation: cFLIPs/vFLIPs function as apoptosis inhibitors with DEDs."];
  "S2" [label="(2,0,0) General Rule: High-damaging strains form hyphae and exacerbate inflammation."];
  "S20" [label="(20,0,0) General Rule: vFLIPs inhibit apoptosis via DED-DED interaction."];
  "S21" [label="(21,0,0) Observation: C. albicans DNA triggers intracellular signaling."];
  "S22" [label="(22,0,0) General Rule: C. albicans proteins not reported to influence intracellular components."];
  "S23" [label="(23,0,0) Phenomenon: Hyphal Als3 interacts with DEDs of FADD/Caspase-8."];
  "S24" [label="(24,0,0) Knowledge: Als3 resembles DED-containing proteins like vFLIPs."];
  "S25" [label="(25,0,0) Knowledge: Intracellular recognition extends immune understanding."];
  "S3" [label="(3,0,0) Observation: C. albicans transitions to opportunistic pathogen in ill patients."];
  "S4" [label="(4,0,0) General Rule: Disseminated candidiasis leads to high mortality (>40%)."];
